{
  "schema": "research-public-artifact/v1",
  "concept": "Salesforce Pub/Sub gRPC subscription flow control and reconnect",
  "slug": "salesforce-pub-sub-grpc-subscription-flow-control-and-reconnect",
  "canonical_concept_id": "concept:1f10c6cde629c92abbadadcba60ad2b9d4b9b9090bc2ea76dfe8e8c5120e79cc",
  "canonical_artifact_sha256": "72f29c8c3824cdf27814a544a809cac43be0b2acca223b168688971d89c3520f",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:8e82abb2e4e8e4e52c1076d06fa14ee10264302ebab6f3ddade7260abd59c246",
      "text": "Subscribe is a bidirectional, pull-based stream. The client grants event demand according to its processing capacity; this provides application-level flow control for a case-alert consumer. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
      "also": [
        "https://mi.docs.wso2.com/en/4.5.0/reference/connectors/sf-pubsub-inbound/sf-pubsub-inbound-endpoint-example/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:138e97d71a85e2e6fbce1c57fd70e54454baa33a831813f19ee6d904d4986742",
        "ev:2983c9f58f9e67dfb86eecdbf1844006f01cd75a30dd8498aca8f23325c287f3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:8367b925597ea7ef84eef73b72340c49fa136f4d926479112e14586ec6c5871d",
      "text": "Additional FetchRequests add demand to undelivered demand on the existing stream. `pending_num_requested` reports events still owed to the client, so use it together with available processing capacity when deciding how much demand to replenish. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/flow-control.html",
      "also": [
        "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:8ee533ff63bec503cf379788c57620c6e0ea3b119f0ee735799fc4feed05deee",
        "ev:a5e7948c108ec00232d61594cf90f4a36d779bcd34a7fc70d9a5c04a764c0203"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:f52c2c0f965a0c33be56c2f221defd40f36bec25128f3daeebeb9b85e534d6bc",
      "text": "When `pending_num_requested` reaches zero, the client must send a new FetchRequest within 60 seconds of the last FetchResponse to keep the subscription stream open. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:357c28d244ae72e50823951fbb56007ddf38789e9d54a1eadea62edb0a7ccc96"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:6c824b7a661c5ac5e7b7803e3db76886cff355e79807507f6542fd02cbf129e7",
      "text": "When `pending_num_requested` is greater than zero but the event bus has no new events to deliver, the server sends an empty FetchResponse as a keepalive within 270 seconds. An empty response therefore does not by itself mean that the stream failed. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/forcedotcom/pub-sub-api/blob/main/pubsub_api.proto"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:0ca556bd36518956d2c168083417884d5354a419da5fe330e1e8a019ac216f90",
        "ev:ccbc5e5937c8914d77300b46f4d31035b6b0e23eb55a83bbf3261ae0cf641f0c"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:782aaf0a6b3b6aca1a0a0966d3c27e00b48452c5392f6032fc55027e4cd67c24",
      "text": "Set `num_requested` to the number of events the consumer can accept. Salesforce documents a maximum request value of 100; the flow-control guide says requests above 100 are treated as 100. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
      "also": [
        "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/flow-control.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:24a9b7af87441660bed23c1d28d0424bb871ccc96fb734c88895e3c3b5bf4bce",
        "ev:b3fb26d25a163c10d1904e40c77b628212479d47e60969c1125f55bb977ed450"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:7c83901675954f772b7222411e7969c88dc98706b02a70f22e98a64d122f2a1d",
      "text": "An RPC error stops the long-lived subscription connection. The client must retry Subscribe to establish another connection; catching the exception alone does not continue delivery. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
      "also": [
        "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/handling-errors.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:68106c14f29fef0c2b59def9ef94910a3d1401366b890dfcbf102f1dd9306407",
        "ev:6965e5698026e6765d7126da3285fbd1f8c466a311189d081c69f72a08e2b90f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:8e3162ccaf0345608187ec8d86e72c52abf37087cb4f381af15849599485b190",
      "text": "Salesforce recommends limiting retry attempts and using exponential backoff for long-lived RPC calls, with recovery behavior selected according to the received error. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/retry-rpc-calls.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:174c999290083ad610f0c9a80d1db1fa0806e6f649236f26189e600fdadbb89b"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:bab018f68991cb11330ab81948c7260da871ba22eba156cf382671fce497cc83",
      "text": "Inspect the custom error code in the gRPC exception trailers through `getTrailers()` to diagnose why the stream failed. Salesforce also supplies an RPC ID for support troubleshooting. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/retry-rpc-calls.html",
      "also": [
        "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/handling-errors.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:58648a600be2de0a40532f62e1d501a5c8b344eecc158d284ec7303958112c31",
        "ev:58ec6ead3e4b2003431883dd38ca934933102b854889f607161543e2dba49dcd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:513a5973a54043a96010f894b92b01c5b12cce6e542d6a39701eb98fea1d7201",
      "text": "An RPC error terminates the long-lived Subscribe stream. The client must retry Subscribe to create a new stream; retry policy depends on the error, and Salesforce recommends limiting attempts and using exponential backoff for transient errors. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/retry-rpc-calls.html",
      "also": [
        "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/handling-errors.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:6965e5698026e6765d7126da3285fbd1f8c466a311189d081c69f72a08e2b90f",
        "ev:ea606b35e20b4d6439aac19085e25fabe183aeaefe39ba9b0d6314ab2a36faf1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:e6eb4ef9921db60d54fe5554b851a9e0919fe916ca7d9e746d086068c6b7372d",
      "text": "The Subscribe reference caps the `num_requested` field in FetchRequest at 100. Treat this as a documented request limit rather than a promise that an application can process that many concurrently. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:b3fb26d25a163c10d1904e40c77b628212479d47e60969c1125f55bb977ed450"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:f962ef073b551f403e97c5b5aa7ab25cd9bd4a292567dc20bd536c23fbb7880c",
      "text": "The pozil Node client exposes requestAdditionalEvents(topicName, numRequested) to add demand on an existing subscription; this is a client-library operation rather than a new RPC connection. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/pozil/pub-sub-api-node-client",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:fb9659545c96a8ca555f2fc4fcf716e13f69f077c20befdd30103a24bbcfc98a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:893877ad8b6becca66ced9d9e77db6eb9eb8de8958293c8720a2a05f85812717",
      "text": "An Apache Camel issue reports that its PubSubApiClient could repeatedly resubscribe with an invalid replay ID, demonstrating why a reconnect loop must classify errors instead of blindly retrying identical input. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CAMEL-21740",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:827b199ef7624cdc716cb783d3e9846e8b95659923daab420874e8a6c9f7b955"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:f645e1bde86d533d763244b5bc15ce252e685454d6c3b9b411c837597b428303",
      "text": "FetchRequest and FetchResponse are not paired one-to-one: a requested event count can be delivered through multiple responses. Replenishment logic must track event capacity rather than assume one response completes one request. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/forcedotcom/pub-sub-api/blob/main/pubsub_api.proto",
      "also": [
        "https://mi.docs.wso2.com/en/4.5.0/reference/connectors/sf-pubsub-inbound/sf-pubsub-inbound-endpoint-example/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:7c74e2e1d676ce54e5c620ef43465d5477aaa6e43e560de3b91b1a0b5b9dd703",
        "ev:aa2e83d7ca96603e9ba9d806b35dd30c5166f048acce4564cd6feb949ecfa7c1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:c3130b1d3c28c139402ea9fa34b4aef50a90f653b853b496ec47194e0aa2c580",
      "text": "A later FetchRequest must keep the original topic_name if it supplies one. A mismatch returns INVALID_ARGUMENT; changing the starting stream position requires a fresh Subscribe RPC. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
      "also": [
        "https://mi.docs.wso2.com/en/4.5.0/reference/connectors/sf-pubsub-inbound/sf-pubsub-inbound-endpoint-example/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:3291a503806867a3027b432b459bfe0245f36ec107bafc602f28ebe01847cbb4",
        "ev:a1a1644108ac7de7842849905255f89559d68588c7bfe6cedb4d1eb02b07000e",
        "ev:db16f4ea89afe02f56d141dc703a3bd6915de9e7faab8e27ae4895b560d9cb8a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:3cf288f48893e0e46001ce30a2ebac55ca614d887e590faea58377907ac2515f",
      "text": "A Subscribe stream keeps one topic: a later FetchRequest may omit `topic_name`, but if present it must match the initial topic. A mismatch returns `INVALID_ARGUMENT`; changing the requested topic requires a separate subscription stream. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/forcedotcom/pub-sub-api/blob/main/pubsub_api.proto",
      "also": [
        "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:a1a1644108ac7de7842849905255f89559d68588c7bfe6cedb4d1eb02b07000e",
        "ev:d2fbf83639a6804a6220949ada77c7550f01ff4708902dddeaa98589a9b012a2"
      ]
    }
  ],
