      "text": "Salesforce Subscribe uses a long-lived, bidirectional stream with client-controlled event demand. A case-alerting subscriber must replenish demand according to processing capacity, distinguish healthy idle keepalives from exhausted demand, and establish a fresh RPC after an error. Official guidance recommends bounded retries with exponential backoff. WSO2 independently documents the pull-based request flow; a reported Apache Camel reconnect loop illustrates the risk of retrying invalid input unchanged. The Node client supplies a concrete demand-replenishment operation.",
